<title>SRI LANKA: SRI LANKA AVERAGE LENDING RATE FALLS TO 13.1 PCT.</title>
<headline>SRI LANKA AVERAGE LENDING RATE FALLS TO 13.1 PCT.</headline>
<dateline>COLOMBO 1997-08-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average prime lending rate of Sri Lanka's commercial banks fell to 13.1 percent in the week ending August 8 from 13.4 percent in the week before, the Central Bank said on Friday.</p>
<p>The bank said in its weekly economic report that the average rate a year ago was 18.4 percent.</p>
</text>
